/** Retrofit batch AV -- upgrading old 2-case (and, for one problem, 0-case) gpe-history problems to
 * the 4-case standard (Sample + boundary + tricky + stress). All solvers below were independently
 * written and verified byte-for-byte against each problem's real official Sample before being trusted
 * to generate new tricky/stress expected output.
 *
 * gpe-10766-antimatter-ray-clearcutting: enumerate every maximal collinear line through each pair of
 *   trees (plus a singleton line per tree, for isolated trees with no collinear partner) as a bitmask
 *   of covered trees, then BFS layer-by-layer over the 2^n coverage-mask space (uniform edge weight 1)
 *   to find the minimum number of lines whose union covers at least m trees.
 * gpe-10906-matrix-decompressing: this problem allows multiple valid answers ("you can output any one
 *   of them"), so instead of matching the real Sample's specific matrix, this is modeled as max-flow
 *   (after subtracting the mandatory 1 from every cell, turning it into an ordinary transportation
 *   problem: source->row_i cap=rowSum[i]-C, row_i->col_j cap=19, col_j->sink cap=colSum[j]-R). The
 *   generated matrix was independently checked to satisfy the exact row/column sums from the real
 *   Sample with all entries in [1,20] -- a legitimate alternate answer, not a byte-for-byte match.
 *   Same pre-existing strict-checker/multi-answer caveat as gpe-10658-is-bigger-smarter in batch AU.
 * gpe-11009-all-in-all: two-pointer subsequence check.
 * gpe-11041-children-s-game: sort numbers (as strings) by the classic "a+b vs b+a" comparator to
 *   maximize the concatenation. NOTE: the real test data has each number on its OWN line (not
 *   space-separated after the count) -- a naive per-line parser silently misparsed this, caught while
 *   verifying against the already-seeded boundary case.
 * gpe-11058-exact-sum: sort prices, two-pointer scan converging inward from both ends on every exact
 *   sum match to find the truly minimal-difference pair (not just the first match found). Despite the
 *   problem statement claiming a blank line after each test case, the real sample shows NO blank line.
 * gpe-11130-the-priest-mathematician: Frame-Stewart four-peg recurrence f(n) = min_k 2*f(k)+(2^(n-k)-1),
 *   computed via a monotonic-pointer sweep (the optimal k is non-decreasing in n) with BigInt, since
 *   f(10000) has thousands of digits. The whole f(0..maxN) table is precomputed once per input file.
 *   Cross-checked against the well-known Frame-Stewart four-peg sequence (1,3,5,9,13,17,25,33,...) for
 *   n=3..8 in addition to matching the real sample's n=1,2,28,64 exactly.
 * gpe-11174-homer-simpson: DP over exact-time-used (dp[i] = max burgers using exactly i minutes),
 *   then the largest reachable time <= t determines both the answer and the minimum wasted time.
 */
